# Protect live schedule data

Live restaurant schedules are production data. Sync/UI code bugs have wiped people (Charles, Eugene) and breaks before.

## Do not touch schedule data unless explicitly asked

Never do any of the following unless the user clearly asks to restore, seed, repair, or edit schedule contents:

- Write/update/delete `schedule_cells`, `schedule_slots`, or team_state schedule blobs (Supabase, scripts, SQL, RPC)
- Flush outbox ops, revive cells, assert/seed weeks, or run restore/seed scripts against a real company
- “Fix” a blank person/row by inventing names, roster defaults, or copying another week into cloud
- Use browser automation to edit the live Schedule grid as a data repair

## Code edits are OK; data writes are not

You may change `app.js` / `schedule-sync-v2.js` sync logic. Do **not** compensate by pushing corrected cells to cloud.

If schedule data looks wrong, **diagnose and report** (who/what week/cloud vs local). Ask before any repair write.

## Safe defaults

- Prefer read-only queries when investigating
- Prefer local/`npm` tests and fixtures over production Supabase mutations
- If a fix requires a one-shot data repair, stop and get explicit approval first

## Cloud is king (sync code)

- Cloud cells win on Refresh and soft peer apply; denser local must not soft-win
- Only conscious interactive edits (or explicit force-push / assert week) may write `set_times` / `set_day_off` / `set_worker`
- Auto-repair, revive, Karl scrub, and seed-missing-weeks must not push to cloud
- Admin and manager share the same cell poll / Refresh SoT path
